Install Cygwin (if "work" will allow that) under
Ms-Windows. and work there. Cygwin _almost_ lets you
forget that MS-Windows exists.

Install a dual boot Linux partition at work and do
your futzing there.

You'll want to use a script to do your compiling
even in a simple case like hello world, so that you
can look at error messages and compare them to what
you thought you told the computer to do. After a
while, you'll want to learn make file writing, which
helps you handle complex projects like NetHack.

